istical power"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "used the dyadic unit which aggregates multiple games, obscuring within-dyad dynamics", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["dyad", "aggregation"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [152]}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "would have preferred a game-level analysis with player/referee random effects for finer-grained inference, but did not use it due to model complexity and convergence issues with rare events", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["game-level model", "random effects"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [151]}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[169, 169]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "found the data cover four European leagues in one season (2012-2013)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dataset scope"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[172, 174]], "note": "caveats on generalizability to other leagues/periods, decisions, sports"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[176, 176]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "explored multiple model forms, thresholds, and covariate sets, and selected the reported specification based on statistical performance (smallest p-value with referee clustering)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["specification search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [160, 161]}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "found this specification-search process introduces researcher degrees of freedom and inflates Type I error risk", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["specification search"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [159, 161]}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "found the robustness checks mitigate this specification-search concern", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness checks"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [159, 160]}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "section separator"}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "intro stating the following choices favor detecting an effect"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[184, 184]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[185, 185]], "assertion": "chose a binary exposure threshold at 0.5, which maximizes sample size in both groups", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["threshold"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [170]}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[185, 185]], "assertion": "found robustness to continuous and extreme-group specifications supports this threshold choice", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [169]}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "found HC1 robust-only standard errors give p=0.0065 versus p=0.0035 with referee clustering, strengthening statistical significance", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors", "p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [173]}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "asserted referee clustering is the correct adjustment for the data structure", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [172]}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "applied no multiplicity adjustment because only a single pre-specified hypothesis was tested", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiplicity adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "found complete-case analysis excluded 15% of dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [178]}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "found missingness appears administrative (photo availability) rather than outcome-dependent, mitigating selection-bias concern", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missingness"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [177]}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "clustered standard errors by referee only, not by player or two-way", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["clustering", "player"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 181, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[195, 195]], "assertion": "used no matching or weighting; regression adjustment assumed linearity and additivity of covariate effects", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["matching", "weighting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[197, 197]], "assertion": "found the effect remains significant and positive across multiple specifications despite these favorable-choice caveats", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "section separator"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[201, 201]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[202, 202]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[203, 203]], "assertion": "concluded the hypothesis status is \"SUPPORTED\"", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "found the data provide statistically significant, directionally consistent evidence supporting the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 193, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 212]], "assertion": "found summary of evidence: primary risk difference 0.21pp, secondary OR 1.19, all sensitivity analyses positive (0.21-0.37pp, p<0.01), 17% relative increase, significance p<0.01", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "odds ratio", "robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 196, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[214, 214]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[215, 215]], "assertion": "found dark-skinned players have approximately 0.2 percentage points higher probability of a red card after adjustment, a substantively meaningful increase given the low base rate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [199]}, {"id": 199, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[215, 215]], "assertion": "found the effect consistent across model specifications and robust to alternative definitions of dark vs light skin", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [198]}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[216, 216]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[217, 217]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 218]], "assertion": "restated this as an exploratory in-sample analysis requiring independent replication with pre-registered methods for confirmatory inference", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exploratory analysis"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [203, 204]}, {"id": 203, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 218]], "assertion": "found unmeasured confounding (e.g., nationality, implicit bias) cannot be ruled out", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [202, 204]}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 218]], "assertion": "found the effect shows heterogeneity by league: strong associations in England and Germany but null effects in Spain and France", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league", "heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [202, 203]}, {"id": 205, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[219, 219]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 206, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[220, 220]], "note": "subheading"}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[221, 224]], "note": "recommended future work not carried out in this analysis (confirmatory replication, causal identification, mechanism testing, generalizability testing)"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[226, 226]], "note": "section separator"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[227, 227]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[228, 228]], "note": "section heading"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[229, 229]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 213, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[230, 230]], "note": "documents data source file, dyad count, and season"}, {"id": 214, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[231, 231]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[232, 232]], "assertion": "used Python 3.11.9, pandas 2.2.2, numpy 1.26.4, statsmodels 0.14.1, and scipy 1.13.1", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 216, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[233, 233]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[234, 234]], "assertion": "set a random seed of 42 a